## 5. Comparison of Methods

| Method | Accuracy | Effort | Why it Works |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Pure LLM Prompt** | Low (~60%) | Minimal | Model "hallucinates" a round number (like 1000). |
| **Chain of Verification** | Medium (85%) | Moderate | Forces the model to look at the beginning and end of the file. |
| **Python/Code Execution** | 100% | High | Uses math/logic instead of text prediction. |

---

## 6. Summary Feedback Mechanism

To build a permanent "fix," use a **multi-agent approach**:
* **Agent A (Executor):** Counts the rows using a script.
* **Agent B (Checker):** Takes the output of Agent A and manually checks the last 5 rows of the CSV to see if the index matches.
* **Feedback:** If Agent B finds a mismatch, it triggers Agent A to re-run the process with a different encoding or delimiter.
